        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T12:37:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The trailing || true drops curl\u0027s exit status, so a download cut off after the 200 status is taken as success: cut at a line break, jq accepts it and the trend silently loses its newest runs. Cut mid-line, an older history is restored instead. Could we keep the status, e.g. || code\u003d\"000 (curl exit $?)\", so a broken transfer ends in the \"failed\" branch like any other unreadable response?",
      "revId": "22c38fd90721e032adfa40cb3b1a897ef8f4832c",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
